# Git workflow

All changes land on `main` through pull requests — never push directly to `main`.

## Branch naming

Lowercase kebab-case with a type prefix:

| Prefix | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| `feature/` | New functionality |
| `fix/` | Bug fixes |
| `chore/` | Tooling, deps, config |
| `docs/` | Documentation only |
| `refactor/` | Behavior-neutral restructure |
| `ci/` | CI/CD changes |

Cursor Cloud Agent branches: `agentic<description>-69a1`.

## Conventional commits

Format: `<type>(<optional scope>): <imperative description>`

Scopes: `website`, `studio`, `cms`, `ui`.

```
feat(website): add work page project grid
fix(cms): require alt text on project images
chore: add cursor rules foundation
```

Rules: imperative mood, ≤ 72 chars, no trailing period. Validated by commitlint on every commit.

## Pull requests

1. Rebase or merge latest `main` before opening.
2. Fill in the PR template completely.
3. One logical change per PR when possible.
4. Include screenshots/recordings for UI changes.
5. Commit `pnpm cms:typegen` output in the same PR as schema changes.

See `CONTRIBUTING.md` for full details.
